Summary: Keep wow64 TEBs and the PEB high in memory, as before Wine 11.18 (Armadillo DRM)
Category: cpu
Kind: fix
Origin: wine-mac-builds
From: written for wine-mac-builds
Source: none published
Upstream: no (the placement changed upstream in Wine 11.18, f0bd9046)
Why: Wine 11.18 (upstream f0bd9046, "Allocate initial TEB and process
 parameters in high memory on 64-bit") stopped reserving the TEB block
 top-down. In wow64 that moved the 32-bit TEBs and the PEB from just under
 2G to the bottom of the address space, next to the main stack. Armadillo,
 the DRM in Big Fish games, then fails to unpack in its child process
 ("General extraction error", hidden behind the activator), so games can't
 be activated. 10.0 and 11.0-11.17 put them high, as Windows 7's wow64
 does. In wow64 only, reserve TEB blocks top-down below 2G again; 64-bit
 processes keep upstream's placement.
Programs: Big Fish games (Armadillo DRM), White Wolf and Waverly Academy
 among them: activation fails with "General extraction error" on Wine 11.18
 and later
Evidence: gmActivator ("###SENDER#BFG_Client_test#GET#PROPERTY_HARDWAREID")
 in a fresh prefix: macfixes 11.22 shows the error and writes no licence;
 10.0 writes 4 HKLM\Software\Licenses values. Its child process makes the
 same calls on both up to the unpack. Either moving the TEB block high or
 not reserving the DOS area (both of which put the TEB and PEB at 0x7ffdx000)
 fixes it on 11.22; the stack stays low in both, so the TEB/PEB is what
 matters.
Status: 2026-11-16: ntdll.so rebuilt from macfixes-11.22 sources with this
 patch; the activator writes its licence (4 values, two runs) instead of
 the error. 32-bit TEB/PEB at 0x7ffda000/0x7ffdd000. Built in wine-macfixes-11.22-build2;
 same result in a fresh prefix.

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
index cc52179..dfa8f2f 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -3875,6 +3875,23 @@ struct thread_data *virtual_alloc_first_thread_data(void)
 }
 
 
+/***********************************************************************
+ *           get_teb_block_placement
+ *
+ * In wow64, reserve TEB blocks top-down below 2G, where Wine 11.17 and
+ * earlier put them (Windows 7's wow64 has them there too). Bottom-up, the
+ * 32-bit TEB and PEB land in low memory next to the stack, and Armadillo's
+ * unpacker then fails with "General extraction error".
+ */
+static unsigned int get_teb_block_placement( ULONG_PTR *limit_high )
+{
+    *limit_high = user_space_wow_limit & ~granularity_mask;
+    if (!user_space_wow_limit) return 0;
+    *limit_high = min( user_space_wow_limit, limit_2g - 1 ) & ~granularity_mask;
+    return MEM_TOP_DOWN;
+}
+
+
 /***********************************************************************
  *           virtual_alloc_first_teb
  */
@@ -3883,6 +3900,8 @@ void virtual_alloc_first_teb(void)
     void *ptr;
     unsigned int status;
     struct file_view *view;
+    ULONG_PTR limit_high;
+    unsigned int alloc_type;
     struct thread_data *data = get_thread_data();
 
     set_large_address_space();
@@ -3892,8 +3911,9 @@ void virtual_alloc_first_teb(void)
     if (is_wow64()) teb_block_size += ROUND_SIZE( 0, sizeof(WOW_TEB), page_mask );
     teb_block_size += page_size;  /* for debug info */
 
-    status = map_view( &view, NULL, 16 * teb_block_size, 0, VPROT_READ | VPROT_WRITE,
-                       0, user_space_wow_limit & ~granularity_mask, 0 );
+    alloc_type = get_teb_block_placement( &limit_high );
+    status = map_view( &view, NULL, 16 * teb_block_size, alloc_type, VPROT_READ | VPROT_WRITE,
+                       0, limit_high, 0 );
     assert( !status );
     teb_block = view->base;
     teb_block_pos = 14;
@@ -3938,9 +3958,11 @@ NTSTATUS virtual_alloc_teb( struct thread_data *data )
         if (!teb_block_pos)
         {
             struct file_view *view;
+            ULONG_PTR limit_high;
+            unsigned int alloc_type = get_teb_block_placement( &limit_high );
 
-            if ((status = map_view( &view, NULL, 32 * teb_block_size, 0, VPROT_READ | VPROT_WRITE,
-                                    0, user_space_wow_limit & ~granularity_mask, 0 )))
+            if ((status = map_view( &view, NULL, 32 * teb_block_size, alloc_type, VPROT_READ | VPROT_WRITE,
+                                    0, limit_high, 0 )))
             {
                 server_leave_uninterrupted_section( &virtual_mutex, &sigset );
                 return status;
